# headwear/helm/masked: the Masked helm (P2c ladder slice, LADDER-HEAD; form8): the Jade people's closed helm. A ribbed
# bowl lit as a sphere (the ribs are seams, N), a lacquered brow band (P) under a wide brow peak (R), a wide flared neck
# guard of metal lames laced in the accent colour, sweeping out beside the jaw (its hem R), and a face mask with a nose ridge and a
# mouth vent (N) that hides the face to a 1 px eye slit on the eye row (N: it glows at T6). '-' masks the hair over the
# bowl; long hair below the neck guard still shows. Light from the top-left: the left planes in step 3, the turn in 2,
# the shadowed right in 1, one glint at the bowl's top-left. Shared by both bodies (D10). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (polish i1, gen_masked.py) a half mask: the eye band open (rows 10-11), so the eyes and brows read in game; the blind
# panel could not read the full mask's face
# (LADDER-HEAD i2, w2/gen_masked2.py) the half mask in profile too: R and L open the eye band (rows 10-11) as D
# does, so the eye and the profile read; the lame lacing dots calmed (the grille read)
# (LADDER-HEAD i3, w3/gen_jade3.py) the neck guard in three short steel lames with one gilt hem (R), no longer
# flared past the head; the cheek and eye band open in R / L (the panel read i2's orange leather stripes as a crate)
use person
body adult
role helm form8
role helm fam.mask
layer headwear
anchor head
keys hatpose
tags overlay


# (FORGE-HELM i2, crown_tweak.py) the crown mark two rows down the dome: the crest rides the dome, never over the frame top (B10)
# (FORGE-HELM i3, crown3.py) mark crown on the top outline row (it sat 2 rows down in the bowl and buried every crest)

view D key rest origin 2 1
mark crown 9 3
