# (FORGE-HEAD envelope r1) A4: the knapped mask helm: big glass facets, the face plate one dark plane, no 1 px seam

# (FORGE-HEAD envelope r2, tools2/knapped2.py) A4: the face opens from the eyes to the chin between glass cheek plates; three knapped facets and one 2 px specular (C19 A4)
# (FORGE-HEAD envelope r3) A4: the profile face open from the eye band to the chin (the front cheek plate gone: the judge saw the side views bury the face), and a 2 x 2 specular low on the bowl under the shard crest (D R L), the glass tell that survives the glint limiter
# (envelope fix round 2, HEAD, bevor.py) D59: the knapped mask's R and L views carry a black-glass bevor under the chin (two rows of step-1 glass, lit only at its top-left end, its bottom outline over the shoulder line): the gorget, cloak-edge and pauldron trims no longer show as a pale bar below the face
